<section id="faq">
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
<details><summary>Can a provider pay for the #1 spot?</summary><p>No. Rankings are ordered by score, and payment never changes a score or a ranking position.</p></details>
<details><summary>How often do you update reviews?</summary><p>We aim to re-check each review every 90 days. The "Last verified" date on each page shows when that last happened.</p></details>
<details><summary>Who funds BeVerified?</summary><p>Affiliate commissions from some provider sign-ups. See How we make money above.</p></details>
<details><summary>Can a provider correct its review?</summary><p>Yes, with a source we can check. Accepted corrections update the facts; the score only moves if the rubric says it should.</p></details>
<details><summary>Does a high score mean a provider is compliant for my business?</summary><p>No. A score reflects our rubric, not a legal opinion. Do your own due diligence before signing a contract.</p></details>
</section>

